# Dual TCP/UDP Multi-Client Server & Benchmark Client

A lightweight Python networking project demonstrating concurrent TCP and UDP servers bound to the same port, paired with a CLI client that measures connection setup time and per-message Round-Trip Time (RTT).

## Features

- **Dual-Protocol Binding:** Runs a multi-threaded TCP server and a UDP datagram listener simultaneously on the same port (`9100` by default).
- **Packet Loss Simulation:** Configurable application-layer UDP drop rate (`--drop-rate`) to test timeout and retry behavior under simulated congestion.
- **Latency Benchmarking:** Measures TCP handshake overhead separately from message RTT.
- **Zero External Dependencies:** Built purely with the Python 3 standard library (`socket`, `socketserver`, `threading`, `argparse`).

## Requirements

- Python 3.9+

